lerta: no name of an executable in std:io: give -o
usage: lerta build [options] <source> [<file>...]

options:
  -o, --output <output>  write the executable here
  --target <target>      build for the target
  -O, --optimize         optimize, without the memory checks unless asked for
  --memory-checks        check memory as the program runs
  --werror               treat warnings as errors
  --no-trace             print no trace of an uncaught exception
  --source-lines         show the lines of the source in traces
  --eager-nan-checks     check for NaN where each operation gives it
  --linker-flag <flag>   pass the flag to the linker
  -h, --help             show this help
